Implemented Vercel Web Analytics configuration for this React/Vite project.

## Changes Made

### Modified Files:
- **package.json**: Added `@vercel/analytics` (v1.6.1) to dependencies

### Updated Lock Files:
- **pnpm-lock.yaml**: Updated with new @vercel/analytics package and dependencies

## Implementation Details

According to the latest Vercel Analytics documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), for React/Vite projects, the Analytics component should be imported from `@vercel/analytics/react` and added to the root App component.

The Analytics component was already properly configured in `src/App.tsx`:
- Import: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/react";`
- Usage: `<Analytics />` component added within the HelmetProvider wrapper

The missing piece was the package installation, which has now been completed.

## Verification

1. ✅ Package installed successfully using pnpm
2. ✅ Build completed successfully without errors
3. ✅ Analytics component is properly placed in the app root
4. ✅ Lock file updated to ensure consistent dependency resolution

## Notes

- The project uses pnpm as its package manager
- Version installed: @vercel/analytics v1.6.1
- The Analytics component is rendered at the root level of the application within the HelmetProvider
- Analytics data will appear in the Vercel dashboard once the application is deployed and users visit the site
- Pre-existing TypeScript errors in the codebase are unrelated to this Analytics integration

## Next Steps

To fully enable analytics:
1. Ensure the project is deployed to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics tab)
3. Analytics data will begin appearing after users visit the deployed site
